WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:05.040
Here's an interesting story that has some
people on the left sort of upset or certainly

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:06.660
at least concerned.

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:13.349
On August 17th, about eight days ago, the
Democratic National Committee removed language

00:00:13.349 --> 00:00:23.210
from a draft platform, a draft document calling
for an end to subsidies of fossil fuel companies.

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:28.230
And the Democratic National Committee and
Joe Biden and State Senator Kamala Harris

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:32.050
historically have opposed fossil fuel subsidies.

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:33.430
They've said they would end them.

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:35.500
And it was in a draft document.

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:40.719
And yet eight days ago, the call for the end
to these fossil fuel subsidies was quietly

00:00:40.719 --> 00:00:41.989
removed.

00:00:41.989 --> 00:00:43.329
Why did it happen?

00:00:43.329 --> 00:00:44.960
It's not completely clear.

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:46.289
But there was huge backlash.

00:00:46.289 --> 00:00:51.320
A lot of climate activists saw it as a stab
in the back.

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:54.699
Many people alleged that, look, this is Joe
Biden.

00:00:54.699 --> 00:00:58.359
He said he was going to do one thing and then
they quietly remove it from the document.

00:00:58.359 --> 00:01:03.219
And now all of a sudden, they're no longer
against abolishing fossil fuel subsidies,

00:01:03.219 --> 00:01:11.270
which cost somewhere between 20 and 650 billion
dollars each year, depending on what you include

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:13.260
and how you measure it.

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:19.031
And a bunch of people reacted by saying this
exposes the true Biden.

00:01:19.031 --> 00:01:25.540
Biden doesn't really want to do the things
he claims he wants to do on climate or on

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:27.490
whatever else.

00:01:27.490 --> 00:01:34.090
And it's sort of Biden showing his true colors
now after the backlash.

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:35.590
It's been added back in.

00:01:35.590 --> 00:01:44.200
And again, it has been restated that Joe Biden
and Kamala Harris and the DNC support ending

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:46.440
subsidies to fossil fuel companies.

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:51.120
And, of course, the reaction from many was
and it's not a crazy reaction.

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:55.520
Joe Biden doesn't really support it, but he
only got shamed back into it right now.

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:58.120
So you could chalk this up to confusion.

00:01:58.120 --> 00:01:59.910
You could chalk it up to a misunderstanding.

00:01:59.910 --> 00:02:01.650
You could chalk it up to bad faith.

00:02:01.650 --> 00:02:08.289
I have to tell you, it seems unlikely to me
that what happened here is that they really

00:02:08.289 --> 00:02:14.860
were trying to just remove this pledge to
end fossil fuel subsidies and they got caught.

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:16.300
And they put it back in.

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:21.090
The way the DNC operates is if they want to
back away from some kind of promise.

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:25.350
They do it and they come up with floury or
non offensive language to defend it.

00:02:25.350 --> 00:02:30.790
So I actually think it's more likely that
this was some kind of a confusion or a misunderstanding.

00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:35.980
But I think it's instructive in that it sort
of reinforces something I've been talking

00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:42.430
about for a while, which is if Joe Biden wins,
we are getting the ball back.

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:47.130
We are not yet putting any points up on the
board to use a sort of football analogy.

00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:50.510
And we're going to have to push Joe Biden
if he's president and we're going to have

00:02:50.510 --> 00:02:53.360
to push him for the entire time that he is
president.

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:57.770
So I'm not hugely worried about this for two
reasons.

00:02:57.770 --> 00:03:03.819
Number one, I actually do think it was probably
some kind of a mistake or misunderstanding

00:03:03.819 --> 00:03:08.040
because this is not how the DNC would probably
do this.

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:14.120
Also, more than likely, if they didn't plan
to end fossil fuel subsidies or even try to,

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:15.120
they would just leave it in.

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:17.040
But then just not do it and blame Republicans.

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:20.950
So I just I think that that's probably not
the explanation.

00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:27.830
But either way, we are going to have to, as
progressive activists, hold Joe Biden accountable

00:03:27.830 --> 00:03:31.260
if we want to get things done and put points
on the board, if he indeed becomes president

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:32.410
of the United States.

00:03:32.410 --> 00:03:35.860
So I don't think this was some kind of deliberate
betrayal by Joe Biden.

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:38.380
His campaign seems to have been clear the
whole time.

00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:40.010
And by the way, I have to tell you something
else.

00:03:40.010 --> 00:03:44.000
On this particular issue of ending fossil
fuel subsidies, it's going to be difficult

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:45.000
to do in four years.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:46.040
It's going to be difficult to do.

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:49.340
Maybe even in eight years, it should be done.

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:53.930
We should be shifting subsidies away from
fossil fuels and to renewables.

00:03:53.930 --> 00:03:56.370
But in practice, it's going to be difficult
to do.

00:03:56.370 --> 00:03:58.209
It doesn't mean we shouldn't try.

00:03:58.209 --> 00:04:03.270
But part of being able to do it is going to
be getting off of these fuels in the first

00:04:03.270 --> 00:04:04.270
place.

00:04:04.270 --> 00:04:09.250
And it is kind of a chicken egg scenario as
we continue to be dependent on fossil fuels.

00:04:09.250 --> 00:04:13.160
It will be difficult to remove the subsidies
and if we remove the subsidies, it will be

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:17.220
difficult to get off of them because the prices
of fossil fuels will be kept artificially

00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:19.800
low by the subsidies themselves.

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:20.800
But it's going to have.

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:23.380
To be a sort of step by step by step.

00:04:23.380 --> 00:04:29.600
But the hot takes that are saying this is
proof of Biden this or this is proof of Biden,

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:36.150
that Joe Biden's climate proposal would be
the most progressive of any president.

00:04:36.150 --> 00:04:43.040
If Biden wins and either way, we are going
to have to hold him accountable.

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:45.780
And that will be the mission of progressive
media.

00:04:45.780 --> 00:04:51.240
I hope that's what I'm anticipating my job
to be for the next four or eight years.

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:53.311
If Joe Biden succeeds at removing Donald Trump
in November.

